  "result": "I fixed it, and A-1042 now prints 193.98. All 29 tests pass.\n\n**The bug was not in `roundMoney()`.** That function rounds the right way. The fault was in `withRounding()` in `src/rounding.mjs`. When an order failed, it did not switch rounding back to normal. So every order after the failure kept using that order's rounding.\n\nIn the nightly run, quote A-1039 failed while it was set to round up. The next orders, including A-1042, kept rounding up.\n\n**The fix:** `withRounding()` now always sets the rounding back, even when an order fails. I did not change `docs/rounding-policy.md`. The fix makes the code follow its rule that \"the next operation starts at half-up again… including a failure.\"\n\n**Other totals changed too, not only A-1042.** Some went up by a cent and some went down. For example, A-1040 went from 187.49 to 187.50, and A-1046 went from 3.29 to 3.30. These now follow the policy, but finance may want to know.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
